      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In a 39-year old woman hospitalized for intracranial hypertension MRI revealed the presence of abnormal areas in the cerebellar cortex. The negative results of investigations for possible causes, as well as the appearance of radiological abnormalities and their persistence over a 6-month period incited the authors to make a tentative diagnosis of Lhermitte-Duclos disease, despite the lack of anatomicopathological evidence."},
